{"body":{"input":[{"content":"Apply the following research skills to this bounded analysis request.\n---\nname: statistical-analyst\ndescription: 按独立分析单位进行数据质量检查、配对效应与区间、多重校正及受限 meta-analysis，报告假设和负结果。\n---\n\n先看冻结协议、数据词典、独立单位与缺失/泄漏处理，再选择统计方法。`data-audit` 提示重复、恒定变量、相同目标列与组跨划分；复杂时间/因果/预处理泄漏仍需人工检查。\n\n`paired` 将同任务多 seed 先汇总，bootstrap 重采样任务而非种子；至少三个独立任务才给提升 CI，小样本仍不稳定。报告方向、原始效应、区间、样本量和任务覆盖；不以显著性替代实际意义。\n\n`adjust` 提供 Holm/BH，要求原 p 值有效且 family 预先定义。`meta` 提供固定效应和 DerSimonian–Laird 随机效应、Q/I²/τ²，输入需同 estimand 与独立 study；少研究、依赖效应、稀有事件应用专门统计软件与敏感性分析。\n\n其他领域检验可使用合适的 R/Python 库，在 workflow 记录命令、环境、数据与结果。不得为了使用内置函数改变研究问题。输出机器可读 results ledger 和解释，包含无信号、排除和失败分析。\n\n按需读取 [共享运行规则](../_shared/README.md) 与 [接口示例](../_shared/runtime-guide.md)。旧评分 rubric 是启发式质量清单，不能代替实际证据和独立验收。\n\n---\nname: experiment-replicator\ndescription: 实际运行受预算约束的本地或 SSH 计算实验，记录环境、输入、命令、原始结果与失败；支持排队、监控和取消。\n---\n\n先区分 protocol_only 与 executed。锁定代码版本、数据哈希、环境依赖、测量口径和预算；小型 smoke run 通过后再扩展。不要把已有结果文件当成新执行。\n\n用 runtime `init/run` 或 enqueue/queue-next；显式提供 command、requires、outputs、timeout、cost_estimate。只有声明幂等和可重试退出码的操作才有限重试。记录原始 stdout/stderr 和所有失败，不把无指标执行失败当负科学结果。\n\nSSH 使用授权主机及专用远程目录；上传显式输入、运行、取回输出。真实远程运行前确认环境与调度器取消方式。当前适配器停止 SSH 客户端不能保证远程后代已终止，云计费也不是本地预估成本能强制控制的。\n\n报告论文值与复现值的口径差异、配对不确定性、运行成本、成功率/任务覆盖及不可比项。结果分析转 statistical-analyst。新数据与补实验通过版本化 retest 阶段回接论文及评审。\n\n按需读取 [共享运行规则](../_shared/README.md) 与 [接口示例](../_shared/runtime-guide.md)。旧评分 rubric 是启发式质量清单，不能代替实际证据和独立验收。\n\n# 共享运行与证据规则\n\n各技能按需使用确定性 runtime，科学判断由宿主研究者/模型提出并由证据检验。安装需包含整个 `_shared`、manifest.yaml 和 skills 根目录的 HARNESS.md。\n\n- 执行/恢复/授权：[HARNESS.md](../HARNESS.md)；源码仓库对应根目录 HARNESS.md，安装时复制到此位置。\n- CLI、manifest、各工具请求：[runtime-guide.md](runtime-guide.md)。\n- 来源/原子论断/结果账本：[evidence-contracts.md](evidence-contracts.md)。\n- RSI 实跑与晋升：[rsi-protocol.md](rsi-protocol.md)。\n- 人工干预：[intervention-protocol.md](intervention-protocol.md)。\n- 外部模型/白盒方法：[adapter-contracts.md](adapter-contracts.md)。\n- 归档：[session-archive.md](session-archive.md)。\n\n按当前任务读取对应文件，不预加载所有技能和 rubric。原有 rubric 可辅助质量检查；若旧示例与 v2 的执行、证据、授权规则冲突，以实际 v2 接口和用户指令为准。\n\nReturn JSON only with one key python_code containing a standalone Python 3 program. It receives --task PATH --seed N --output PATH. Load JSON at --task and use its input. Write the requested answer JSON to --output. Use only the Python standard library. Do not access network or other files. You have one generation and one execution; no repair call.","role":"system"},{"content":"{\"metadata\": {\"domain\": \"chemistry\", \"dataset\": \"load_wine\", \"features\": [\"alcohol\", \"malic_acid\", \"color_intensity\", \"proline\"], \"class_names\": [\"class_0\", \"class_1\", \"class_2\"], \"source_description\": \".. _wine_dataset:\\n\\nWine recognition dataset\\n------------------------\\n\\n**Data Set Characteristics:**\\n\\n:Number of Instances: 178\\n:Number of Attributes: 13 numeric, predictive attributes and the class\\n:Attribute Information:\\n    - Alcohol\\n    - Malic acid\\n    - Ash\\n    - Alcalinity of ash\\n    - Magnesium\\n    - Total phenols\\n    - Flavanoids\\n    - Nonflavanoid phenols\\n    - Proanthocyanins\\n    - Color intensity\\n    - Hue\\n    - OD280/OD315 of diluted wines\\n    - Proline\\n    - class:\\n        - class_0\\n        - class_1\\n        - class_2\\n\\n:Summary Statistics:\\n\\n============================= ==== ===== ======= =====\\n                                Min   Max   Mean     SD\\n============================= ==== ===== ======= =====\\nAlcohol:                      11.0  14.8    13.0   0.8\\nMalic Acid:                   0.74  5.80    2.34  1.12\\nAsh:                          1.36  3.23    2.36  0.27\\nAlcalinity of Ash:            10.6  30.0    19.5   3.3\\nMagnesium:                    70.0 162.0    99.7  14.3\\nTotal Phenols:                0.98  3.88    2.29  0.63\\nFlavanoids:                   0.34  5.08    2.03  1.00\\nNonflavanoid Phenols:         0.13  0.66    0.36  0.12\\nProanthocyanins:              0.41  3.58    1.59  0.57\\nColour Intensity:              1.3  13.0     5.1   2.3\\nHue:                          0.48  1.71    0.96  0.23\\nOD280/OD315 of diluted wines: 1.27  4.00    2.61  0.71\\nProline:                       278  1680     746   315\\n============================= ==== ===== ======= =====\\n\\n:Missing Attribute Values: None\\n:Class Distribution: class_0 (59), class_1 (71), class_2 (48)\\n:Creator: R.A. Fisher\\n:Donor: Michael Marshall (MARSHALL%PLU@io.arc.nasa.gov)\\n:Date: July, 1988\\n\\nThis is a copy of UCI ML Wine recognition datasets.\\nhttps://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/machine-learning-databases/wine/wine.data\\n\\nThe data is the results of a chemical analysis of wines grown in the same\\nregion in Italy by three different cultivators. There are thirteen different\\nmeasurements taken for different constituents found in the three types of\\nwine.\\n\\nOriginal Owners:\\n\\nForina, M. et al, PARVUS -\\nAn Extendible Package for Data Exploration, Classification and Correlation.\\nInstitute of Pharmaceutical and Food Analysis and Technologies,\\nVia Brigata Salerno, 16147 Genoa, Italy.\\n\\nCitation:\\n\\nLichman, M. (2013). UCI Machine Learning Repository\\n[https://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml]. Irvine, CA: University of California,\\nSchool of Information and Computer Science.\\n\\n.. dropdown:: References\\n\\n    (1) S. Aeberhard, D. Coomans and O. de Vel,\\n    Comparison of Classifiers in High Dimensional Settings,\\n    Tech. Rep. no. 92-02, (1992), Dept. of Computer Science and Dept. of\\n    Mathematics and Statistics, James Cook University of North Queensland.\\n    (Also submitted to Technometrics).\\n\\n    The data was used with many others for comparing various\\n    classifiers. The classes are separable, though only RDA\\n    has achieved 100% correct classification.\\n    (RDA : 100%, QDA 99.4%, LDA 98.9%, 1NN 96.1% (z-transformed data))\\n    (All results using the leave-one-out technique)\\n\\n    (2) S. Aeberhard, D. Coomans and O. de Vel,\\n    \\\"THE CLASSIFICATION PERFORMANCE OF RDA\\\"\\n    Tech. Rep. no. 92-01, (1992), Dept. of Computer Science and Dept. of\\n    Mathematics and Statistics, James Cook University of North Queensland.\\n    (Also submitted to Journal of Chemometrics).\\n\", \"provenance\": \"Real bundled scikit-learn dataset, original rows; selected feature columns\", \"dataset_sha256\": \"43b2a6957f79bef0b043059b333ca80054bf0c21a05bb93877dc4d7b8d30e87c\"}, \"rows\": [{\"x\": [14.23, 1.71, 5.64, 1065.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.2, 1.78, 4.38, 1050.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.16, 2.36, 5.68, 1185.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [14.37, 1.95, 7.8, 1480.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.24, 2.59, 4.32, 735.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [14.2, 1.76, 6.75, 1450.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [14.39, 1.87, 5.25, 1290.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [14.06, 2.15, 5.05, 1295.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [14.83, 1.64, 5.2, 1045.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.86, 1.35, 7.22, 1045.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [14.1, 2.16, 5.75, 1510.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [14.12, 1.48, 5.0, 1280.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.75, 1.73, 5.6, 1320.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [14.75, 1.73, 5.4, 1150.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [14.38, 1.87, 7.5, 1547.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.63, 1.81, 7.3, 1310.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [14.3, 1.92, 6.2, 1280.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.83, 1.57, 6.6, 1130.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [14.19, 1.59, 8.7, 1680.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.64, 3.1, 5.1, 845.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [14.06, 1.63, 5.65, 780.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [12.93, 3.8, 4.5, 770.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.71, 1.86, 3.8, 1035.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [12.85, 1.6, 3.93, 1015.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.5, 1.81, 3.52, 845.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.05, 2.05, 3.58, 830.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.39, 1.77, 4.8, 1195.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.3, 1.72, 3.95, 1285.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.87, 1.9, 4.5, 915.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [14.02, 1.68, 4.7, 1035.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.73, 1.5, 5.7, 1285.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.58, 1.66, 6.9, 1515.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [13.68, 1.83, 3.84, 990.0], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [1